.TH GETSPNAM_R 3
.SH NAME
getspnam_r, getspent_r, fgetspent_r, sgetspent_r \- reentrant shadow password database access
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <shadow.h>
.PP
.BI "int getspnam_r(const char *" name ", struct spwd *" spbuf ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct spwd **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int getspent_r(struct spwd *" spbuf ", char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ,
.BI "struct spwd **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int fgetspent_r(FILE *" stream ", struct spwd *" spbuf ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct spwd **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int sgetspent_r(const char *" string ", struct spwd *" spbuf ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct spwd **" result ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are the reentrant equivalents of the shadow-password lookups.  Each parses
an
.I /etc/shadow
entry into the caller-supplied
.I spbuf
structure, whose string members point into the caller-supplied scratch buffer
.I buf
(length
.IR buflen ).
On success
.I *result
is set to
.IR spbuf ;
otherwise it is NULL.
.TP
.B getspnam_r
looks the entry up by login
.IR name .
.TP
.B getspent_r
returns the next entry from the stream positioned by
.BR setspent (3)/ endspent (3).
.TP
.B fgetspent_r
reads the next entry from an already-open
.IR stream .
.TP
.B sgetspent_r
parses a single shadow line passed in
.IR string .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success, including the not-found case (where
.I *result
is NULL).  A nonzero error number is returned on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ERANGE
.I buf
was too small to hold the entry.
.TP
.B EINVAL
A NULL argument, or
.B sgetspent_r
was given a malformed line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getspnam (3),
.BR getpwnam_r (3),
.BR shadow (5)
.SH STANDARDS
GNU extension.
